Team assignment with the candidates' weeks at the weekly cap, on the built contracts of abako-dev/contracts#24 at e218b0c,
run in the embedded provider's runtime (pallet-contracts 51, 1 MiB of contract memory).
Each PROBE line is printed by a temporary provider test. It deploys Dao alone, registers a coordinator and the candidates,
and fills every week of every candidate with one reservation of one minute a round, raising the capacity by one each round.
It then calls assign_team, the Dao part of an approval, as the controller with the provider's execution gas (128 MiB of
proof) for one milestone with one requirement, and rolls it back. 'at 31' has one minute free in every week: the first
line needs every week of every candidate, the second only the first week. 'at the cap' has 32 reservations in every week.
An ordinary Kreivo transaction gets 2,446,677 bytes of proof.

